 succeeded in 1806ms:
   1: """The shared assertions. An instrument routes through these instead of remembering to.
   2: 
   3: WHY THIS FILE AND NOT ANOTHER REGISTRY ENTRY. The heredoc class was breached NINE TIMES by
   4: an author who had just read the rule, and the tenth attempt was stopped by a hook that does
   5: not care whether anyone understands it. Fifty-five documented classes is more than anyone
   6: holds. What refuses is what controls.
   7: 
   8: TWO ASSERTIONS, BOTH DRAWN FROM DEFECTS THAT ACTUALLY RECURRED TONIGHT.
   9: 
  10: `require_controls` -- THE ACCUSING DIRECTION.
  11:     Four wrong accusations in one night: 0.06 and 1.79 read out of a WITHDRAWAL NOTICE and
  12:     relayed to a reader; `pool_broken` reported against a pool that was withdrawn on
  13:     purpose; two unbacked-claim findings against the flagship that were not unbacked; a
  14:     count of 49 never-taken branches from an extraction that captured code spans. Every one
  15:     was caught by a person reading the instance. NONE was caught by the instrument.
  16: 
  17:     So the reading becomes part of the instrument. An instrument that reports a corpus-wide
  18:     finding declares a POSITIVE control -- a real corpus item whose answer is already
  19:     established -- and, where the failure mode is over-flagging, a NEGATIVE control it must
  20:     NOT flag. If either disagrees, NOTHING IS PRINTED. A detector that can only say yes is
  21:     not a detector, and the malaria false positive is why the negative side is not optional.
  22: 
  23: `zero_has_a_reading` -- CLASS 52.
  24:     A check reporting zero has two readings and only one is reassuring: "looked, found
  25:     none" and "the marker does not exist so nothing could ever match". Three instances in
  26:     one night, TWO OF THEM INSIDE `regression_check.py`, one of those in its BLOCKING set,
  27:     reporting 0 on every run this project has ever made -- where the zero meant the marker
  28:     was absent from the corpus entirely and was read as "no page has this defect".
  29: 
  30:     A zero is only reportable if the thing being searched FOR is known to exist somewhere.
  31:     When it is not, the answer is NOT_ASSESSABLE, which is a different word on purpose.
  32: 
  33: NEITHER FUNCTION PRINTS A REASSURANCE IT CANNOT SUPPORT. Both raise SystemExit, because a
  34: warning an operator can ignore is the control that has already failed.
  35: """
  36: import sys
  37: 
  38: 
  39: class ControlFailed(SystemExit):
  40:     pass
  41: 
  42: 
  43: def require_controls(instrument, positive, negative=None, out=None):
  44:     """Refuse to proceed unless the known answers come back known.
  45: 
  46:     positive -- (label, actual, expected). A real corpus item whose answer is established
  47:                 independently of this instrument. Established means read from a
  48:                 registration, a delivered page, or a prior recorded finding -- NOT inferred
  49:                 by the same logic under test, which would only prove the code agrees with
  50:                 itself.
  51:     negative -- (label, actual, must_not_be). The case the instrument must NOT flag. Supply
  52:                 it whenever the instrument can over-flag, which is nearly always.
  53: 
  54:     Returns None on success. Raises ControlFailed otherwise, before any count is printed.
  55:     """
  56:     say = out or (lambda s: sys.stdout.write(s + "\n"))
  57:     plab, pact, pexp = positive
  58:     say("CONTROL (positive) %s: %s -> %r, expected %r" % (instrument, plab, pact, pexp))
  59:     if pact != pexp:
  60:         raise ControlFailed(
  61:             "REFUSED: %s does not reproduce the one answer that is already established "
  62:             "(%s gave %r, not %r). It is not trusted for anything else and NO COUNT IS "
  63:             "PRINTED." % (instrument, plab, pact, pexp))
  64:     if negative is None:
  65:         say("CONTROL (negative) %s: NONE DECLARED -- this instrument can only say yes."
  66:             % instrument)
  67:         return
  68:     nlab, nact, nforbid = negative
  69:     say("CONTROL (negative) %s: %s -> %r, must not be %r" % (instrument, nlab, nact, nforbid))
  70:     if nact == nforbid:
  71:         raise ControlFailed(
  72:             "REFUSED: %s FLAGS THE CASE IT MUST NOT (%s came back %r). Accusing in the "
  73:             "wrong direction is the failure this control exists to catch. NO COUNT IS "
  74:             "PRINTED." % (instrument, nlab, nact))
  75:     say("    both controls held.")
  76: 
  77: 
  78: def zero_has_a_reading(count, marker_exists_somewhere, what, where):
  79:     """Return a reportable string for a count, or NOT_ASSESSABLE when a zero is ambiguous.
  80: 
  81:     marker_exists_somewhere -- True only if the thing searched FOR has been observed at
  82:     least once, anywhere, in this run. Not "the vocabulary is non-empty"; the vocabulary
  83:     being non-empty is what `arni_hf_protocol` had.
  84:     """
  85:     if count > 0:
  86:         return "%d %s in %s" % (count, what, where)
  87:     if marker_exists_somewhere:
  88:         return "0 %s in %s -- LOOKED AND FOUND NONE (the marker occurs elsewhere, so the " \
  89:                "search is live)" % (what, where)
  90:     return "NOT_ASSESSABLE: 0 %s in %s, AND THE MARKER OCCURS NOWHERE AT ALL. This zero " \
  91:            "means the search cannot match, not that the defect is absent." % (what, where)
  92: 
  93: 
  94: def refuse_unless_marker_lives(marker, corpus_hits, fixture_hit, instrument):
  95:     """A marker-keyed check must be able to fire. Raise if it provably cannot.
  96: 
  97:     `arni_hf_protocol` was in `regression_check.py`'s BLOCKING set and appears on 0 of 888
  98:     pages. It has reported clean on every run this project has ever made and could not have
  99:     reported anything else.
 100:     """
 101:     if corpus_hits or fixture_hit:
 102:         return
 103:     raise ControlFailed(
 104:         "REFUSED: %s keys on %r, which occurs on NO page in the corpus and in NO fixture. "
 105:         "The check cannot fire. A clean result from it is not evidence." % (instrument, marker))
 106: 
 107: def same_bytes(a_bytes, b_bytes):
 108:     """Compare DELIVERED bytes to LOCAL bytes. Both arguments must already be `bytes`.
 109: 
 110:     READ BYTES, COMPARE BYTES -- CLASS: THE INSTRUMENT NORMALISED WHAT IT WAS MEASURING.
 111:     ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 112:     A page was reported to Mahmood as a deploy gap, and the report had to be withdrawn. The
 113:     evidence was that local content differed from `origin/main` by 752 bytes on a file git
 114:     reported unmodified. The mechanism was the reader, not the repo:
 115: 
 116:         io.open(name, encoding="utf-8").read()   -> TEXT mode, converts CRLF to LF
 117:         git show origin/main:name                -> raw bytes, CRLF preserved
 118: 
 119:     752 was the line count. The two were identical. Worse, the same artefact was used to
 120:     argue the local tree was a MIXTURE OF BUILDS -- which is a frightening claim, because one
 121:     passing spot-check would then license trusting a corpus that could not be trusted -- and
 122:     it was false. Read in binary, local equalled origin on 156 of 157 pages.
 123: 
 124:     THE CORPUS *WAS* A MIXTURE, JUST NOT IN THE WAY THE BROKEN READ SUGGESTED: 133 pages
 125:     carried generator `a3c7bb8b2` and 7 carried the current one. A real finding was nearly
 126:     buried under a fake one produced by the instrument.
 127: 
 128:     So: open in "rb", or `git show` into bytes, and compare bytes. If a comparison must be
 129:     newline-insensitive, normalise BOTH sides explicitly and say so -- never let one side be
 130:     normalised by the mode the file happened to be opened in.
 131:     """
 132:     if not isinstance(a_bytes, bytes) or not isinstance(b_bytes, bytes):
 133:         raise ControlFailed(
 134:             "REFUSED: same_bytes was handed %s and %s, not bytes. A str argument means the "
 135:             "caller already read in text mode, which is the defect this function exists to "
 136:             "prevent -- the newline conversion has happened before the comparison."
 137:             % (type(a_bytes).__name__, type(b_bytes).__name__))
 138:     return a_bytes == b_bytes
 139: 
 140: 
 141: def plant_and_require(instrument, detector, clean_case, planted_case):
 142:     """THE HOUSE REQUIREMENT FOR GATES: plant the defect, require the gate to find it.
 143: 
 144:     Three gates earned their result this way -- the bypass mutant that strips the render-point
 145:     transform, the dead link planted in a synthetic hub, the known-bad input handed to the
 146:     pass/fail audit. Each of the three was written after a gate had already shipped that could
 147:     only say yes. A pre-push hook once printed "Regression check PASS" at 0 of 1522 fully-ok,
 148:     because nothing in it could return non-zero.
 149: 
 150:     A GATE THAT HAS NEVER BEEN SEEN TO FAIL IS NOT A GATE. It is a log line. `detector` is
 151:     called on both cases; it must be quiet on `clean_case` and must fire on `planted_case`,
 152:     and this refuses before the gate is allowed to report anything about real data.
 153:     """
 154:     if detector(planted_case) and not detector(clean_case):
 155:         return
 156:     raise ControlFailed(
 157:         "REFUSED: %s did not survive its planted control -- it %s on the planted defect and "
 158:         "%s on the clean case. A gate that cannot be seen to fail cannot be trusted when it "
 159:         "passes." % (instrument,
 160:                      "fired" if detector(planted_case) else "STAYED QUIET",
 161:                      "fired" if detector(clean_case) else "stayed quiet"))
 162: 
 163: 
 164: def scan_covers_what_it_emits(function_name, own_literals_matched, callee_renders, what):
 165:     """A LITERAL CAN LIVE ONE CALL AWAY, AND A SCAN OF A FUNCTION'S OWN BODY IS NOT A SCAN OF
 166:     WHAT IT EMITS. Same family as `composed_or_stored`, one level up.
 167: 
 168:     THE INCIDENT, 2026-08-23. An audit was written to find procedural sentences asserted from
 169:     literals rather than projected from fields. It filtered to "functions that emit markup" by
 170:     looking for HTML tags among each function's OWN string constants -- and missed
 171:     `protocol_card`, THE FUNCTION IT WAS WRITTEN FOR. That function holds only the sentences;
 172:     it returns `kv_card(...)`, and the tags live in the callee.
 173: 
 174:     The hand-classified control caught it, which is the only reason it was caught: a scan that
 175:     cannot see the known instance cannot be trusted to report an absence.
 176: 
 177:     THE FAMILY THIS BELONGS TO, now six deep in one day: the fix, the probe, or the scan lands
 178:     where the author was looking rather than where the text is produced.
 179: 
 180:         composed at render time, or stored          -- the value was baked into the object
 181:         one render point of two                     -- seven panels used a different callable
 182:         two surfaces of three de-indexed            -- audit_table.html was never touched
 183:         a probe keyed to what the fix removed       -- braces, not field names
 184:         a selector keyed to the defect              -- shrank as the work succeeded
 185:         a scan of a body, not of what it emits      -- THIS ONE
 186: 
 187:     THE CHECK: when classifying functions by what they render, ask whether rendering happens
 188:     HERE or in something this calls. If a function's content is handed to a builder, the scan
 189:     must follow the call or key on the handoff, not on tags.
 190:     """
 191:     if own_literals_matched or callee_renders:
 192:         return
 193:     raise ControlFailed(
 194:         "REFUSED: %s classified `%s` as non-emitting on the strength of its own literals, but "
 195:         "it hands its content to a renderer. A scan of a function's body is not a scan of what "
 196:         "it emits." % (what, function_name))
